Memory cap      : 8 GiB (`Limits::new().with_max_memory_bytes(...)`)
cjxl binary     : ~/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl (--num_threads 1)
Decoders        : jxl 0.4.0 (jxl-rs PRIMARY), jxl-oxide 0.12.5 imazen/fd4e2c3 fork (cross-check)
Metric libs     : butteraugli 0.9, fast-ssim2 0.7.1
Feature set     : __internal_recon_hook butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel

Question
--------
Does the buttloop's internal-recon score (the target it converges
toward) match the score of the SHIPPED bitstream as decoded by the
real decoder? If yes within noise, W44-138 P-1 (per-iter sharpness
recompute) has NEGLIGIBLE quality EV — pivot to perf/architecture.
If no, P-1 is correctness-critical.

Method
------
Per cell, four (bfly, ssim2) scores:
  1. INTERNAL: source vs buttloop's last-iter `InternalRecon` (linear-RGB
     captured via `__recon_hook`, gated on `__internal_recon_hook`
     feature). Cropped, planar; converted to interleaved for metric calls.
  2. DECODED: source vs jxl-rs decode of SHIPPED JXL bitstream
     (linear-RGB derived from sRGB f32 → srgb_to_linear_val).
  3. OXIDE: source vs jxl-oxide decode (request_color_encoding
     `srgb_linear`). Cross-decoder sanity.
  4. CJXL: source vs jxl-rs decode of cjxl-encoded bitstream at the
     same (effort, distance). Reference target framing.

Source-side preprocessing identical to W44-138 / W44-170 harnesses:
  - PNG → u8 sRGB via `image` crate (`to_rgb8`).
  - sRGB u8 → linear-RGB f32 (gamma-2.4 / linear-segment piecewise,
    matching cjxl + jxl-oxide).

Per-cell columns (TSV):
  image, distance, effort, width, height, notes,
  bfly_internal, bfly_decoded, bfly_oxide, bfly_cjxl,
  ssim2_internal, ssim2_decoded, ssim2_oxide, ssim2_cjxl,
  delta_bfly_internal_vs_decoded, delta_bfly_decoded_vs_cjxl,
  delta_ssim2_internal_vs_decoded, delta_ssim2_decoded_vs_cjxl,
  ours_bytes, cjxl_bytes, ours_encode_ms, cjxl_encode_ms, status

Cells (12; all e=8 — buttloop is gated at `effort >= 8` so e7 cells
